Subject: [PATCH 06893/11362] [outer-loop] ARC sk48 round-6: honest null,
 clarifies the carry-mechanic subtlety

Round-6 codex gpt-5.6-sol attempt on sk48 reconfirms the level-3 wall
(now 6 rounds running) but clarifies the carry mechanic precisely: the
magenta-headed chain carries a colored block only when its endpoint has
passed FULLY BEYOND the block -- mere visual overlap during extension is
insufficient, a subtlety not previously documented. Tested forward
target-order, endpoint-clearance, retraction/extension, and reverse-order
variants; none advanced past level 2.

Honest null -- no registry count change, frontier stays at level 2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
